# charon integration step 41 after 546078ea5d: commit ca6e5e9d827ad2b8497b74f313dff20193efbc42
# first parent ac69a1513c8707bea69389b4794e41ef1032e5b3
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: partial monomorphization keeps field projections on the specialized ADT
#
# A field projection names the ADT it projects out of (FieldProjKind::Adt). In the
# instance of a body whose closure type got specialized (closures keep their parent's
# trait clauses), the projected place's type was rewritten to the specialized closure
# but the projection still named the generic one, so Aeneas's interpreter rejected the
# instance body (InterpPaths.project_value sanity check). Rewrite the projection's id
# from the projected place's type after the type was specialized.
#
# The typecheck now checks that a field projection names the ADT of the place it
# projects out of, including the places read by an rvalue (visit_rvalue does not
# recurse into them, so no place of an rvalue was checked before).
#
# Test: ui/monomorphize-mut-closure-field-projection.rs (a closure capturing a closure
# that captures `&mut S`, as chelis's catch_lowering_with did) fails the check without
# the rewrite. monomorphize-mut-opaque(-hard).out: the generic closure type
# `external::closure` was retained only by such a projection in the body of its
# instance, and is gone.

